Fairness note: the backlog is divided exactly equally by item count (9 issues per person). Story-point totals may differ because the SRS requirements have different complexity. Treat these as estimates to discuss as a team; if your instructor expects equal effort as well as equal item count, rebalance ownership after team estimation while preserving clear owners.

6. Issue template to copy into GitHub

Use this format for each GitHub Issue. Replace the example values with the specific requirement.

Title: [IPP-F-001] Role-based registration with email verification

User story:

As a [user role], I want [capability], so that [benefit].

Description:

Implement the requirement described in SRS v1.0 for this requirement ID.

Acceptance criteria:

• List observable conditions that must be satisfied.

• Include the SRS acceptance criterion/test case where applicable.

• Include relevant error and security cases.

Requirement ID: IPP-F-001

Priority: High

Story Points: 5 (enter this in the Project's Story Points field)

Assignee: assigned team member

Sprint: Sprint 1 (select the relevant iteration/field)

